meta {
  name: api-tests
}

auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Ice Cream Inventory API

  Bruno collection for the Delivergate assessment backend.

  ## Run order

  1. Select the `Local` environment.
  2. Run the `Auth > Login` request first. It stores the JWT in the runtime
     variable `token`, which the collection-level Bearer auth uses.
  3. Run the remaining requests. `Create Item` and `Create Customer` store the
     new record IDs in `itemId` and `customerId` for the follow-up requests.

  Running the whole collection with `bru run` executes everything in sequence,
  including cleanup/logout.

  ## Seed credentials

  The `Local` environment uses the values from `backend/.env`:

  | Role    | Email              | Password      |
  | ------- | ------------------ | ------------- |
  | Owner   | owner@mail.com     | Owner@123     |
  | Manager | manager@mail.com   | Manager@123   |
  | Cashier | cashier@mail.com   | Cashier@123   |

  If your `SEED_*` variables differ, update `environments/Local.bru`.
}
